# USC-II reduction: 54–69 species with ignition and flame validation

## Outcome

**The compact mechanism has 54 species and 392 reactions, reducing the supplied 111-species/784-reaction mechanism by 51.35% and 50.00%, respectively.** Across 108 reserved cases, its maximum absolute errors relative to the parent are **4.50% for ignition delay and 2.48% for laminar flame speed**. All reserved cases completed and met the predeclared 10% ignition / 5% flame-speed targets.

These are reductions designed during this run from the supplied parent. Retained rate coefficients, thermodynamic polynomials and transport parameters were copied unchanged. No existing reduced mechanism was downloaded or presented as a new design.

