Use **54 species for the strongest compression**, or **56 species for a small additional cost and lower flame-speed error over much of the tested domain**. The 69-species version provides another measured trade-off; increasing size did not improve every observable. These are exploratory candidates, not evidence of global optimality.

Each row covers **78 ignition and 30 flame cases**, with no failures, censored delays, classification mismatches, missing reference cases, or tolerance violations. Reserved ignition terminal-temperature differences were below 0.70 K; refined flame burned-temperature differences were below 0.45 K. The paired values, signed percentage errors and symmetric logarithmic/factor errors are in [final_analysis/paired.csv](outputs/final_analysis/paired.csv).

